247
00:18:33,247 --> 00:18:34,227
Try to vomit.

248
00:18:34,627 --> 00:18:35,567
Then you'll feel better.

249
00:18:38,247 --> 00:18:39,187
Oh, boy.

250
00:18:39,467 --> 00:18:40,947
Don't you know how to throw up?

251
00:18:41,447 --> 00:18:42,807
Fine, I'll do it.

252
00:18:43,167 --> 00:18:44,447
But don't bite my fingers.

253
00:18:46,027 --> 00:18:47,147
Open wide now.

254
00:18:47,147 --> 00:18:49,627
There you go.

255
00:18:54,207 --> 00:18:55,147
There, there.

256
00:18:55,427 --> 00:18:56,367
You'll be fine.

257
00:18:56,687 --> 00:19:00,147
She saw exactly how pathetic I was right from the start.

258
00:19:01,367 --> 00:19:02,907
So I can't gloss it over.

259
00:19:05,707 --> 00:19:06,547
Hello there.

260
00:19:07,087 --> 00:19:08,907
Do you still have hemp twigs?

261
00:19:09,327 --> 00:19:10,187
I sure do.

262
00:19:10,527 --> 00:19:11,467
Are you just starting?

263
00:19:11,647 --> 00:19:12,807
The sun's about to set.

264
00:19:13,067 --> 00:19:13,867
Yes, you're right.

265
00:19:14,327 --> 00:19:16,087
The shopping took us longer than I thought.

266
00:19:16,087 --> 00:19:20,347
Let's hurry.

267
00:19:20,567 --> 00:19:22,267
It's even later than I thought it was.

268
00:19:22,467 --> 00:19:22,827
Okay.

269
00:19:28,707 --> 00:19:30,807
Hina, go and get us a baking dish.

270
00:19:31,047 --> 00:19:31,807
And some matches.

271
00:19:32,087 --> 00:19:32,427
Okay.

272
00:19:32,427 --> 00:19:32,527
Okay.

273
00:19:32,527 --> 00:19:47,227
Oh, it's lit.

274
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:49,147
No, no.

275
00:19:49,147 --> 00:19:50,147
Don't touch it, Momo.

276
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:51,547
That's what I could smell.

277
00:19:52,607 --> 00:19:54,127
You could smell it all through town.

278
00:19:56,087 --> 00:19:57,307
These are the horses?

279
00:19:57,667 --> 00:19:58,067
Yes.

280
00:19:58,307 --> 00:20:00,647
They ride these little horses to get back home.

281
00:20:00,927 --> 00:20:02,247
For grandma and your mom.

282
00:20:02,507 --> 00:20:02,887
Huh?

283
00:20:02,887 --> 00:20:05,967
But you don't know about it yet.

284
00:20:08,267 --> 00:20:09,227
It figures.

285
00:20:09,707 --> 00:20:10,667
How would you know?

286
00:20:11,987 --> 00:20:13,647
We've made these every year.

287
00:20:14,427 --> 00:20:17,247
My mother and her mother before her all made them.

288
00:20:17,847 --> 00:20:19,327
It's our family tradition.

289
00:20:19,327 --> 00:20:21,207
So that's what we do, too.

290
00:20:23,547 --> 00:20:25,447
Thank you for starving.

291
00:20:25,687 --> 00:20:26,607
Yummy food.

292
00:20:26,847 --> 00:20:27,627
Hurry up.

293
00:20:27,827 --> 00:20:29,087
Give us a little more than usual.

294
00:20:30,047 --> 00:20:32,087
Where are your parents buried, Ray?

295
00:20:32,187 --> 00:20:32,687
Do you know?

296
00:20:35,687 --> 00:20:36,627
In Nagano.

297
00:20:37,107 --> 00:20:38,387
That's my dad's hometown.

298
00:20:38,387 --> 00:20:44,387
I see.

299
00:20:44,647 --> 00:20:45,567
That's far away.

300
00:20:49,087 --> 00:20:49,887
All right.

301
00:20:50,047 --> 00:20:51,187
Dinner's ready, everyone.

302
00:20:51,547 --> 00:20:52,007
Great.

303
00:20:52,467 --> 00:20:53,427
Then let's eat.

304
00:20:55,947 --> 00:20:56,427
Delicious.

305
00:20:56,707 --> 00:20:57,847
Just the way I like it.

306
00:20:58,247 --> 00:20:59,587
Hina did most of the frying.

307
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:00,787
Not bad.

308
00:21:00,927 --> 00:21:02,487
The oil burned me right here.

309
00:21:02,827 --> 00:21:03,427
Oh, dear.

310
00:21:03,667 --> 00:21:05,167
That's the problem with hot oil.

311
00:21:05,327 --> 00:21:06,367
Better take care of that.

312
00:21:06,847 --> 00:21:07,887
Go get the ointment.

313
00:21:08,387 --> 00:21:10,067
It's in one of my drawers somewhere.

314
00:21:10,687 --> 00:21:13,427
There's no reminiscing about the past during this dinner.

315
00:21:15,287 --> 00:21:18,267
This family's wounds are too fresh to even go there.

316
00:21:19,187 --> 00:21:20,487
They're not ready yet.

317
00:21:28,487 --> 00:21:30,187
What was it like for me again?

318
00:21:32,627 --> 00:21:34,207
When did I stop crying?

319
00:21:34,207 --> 00:21:39,327
How long did it take for me to pull it together?

320
00:21:42,007 --> 00:21:42,887
It's strange.

321
00:21:43,447 --> 00:21:44,627
I can't even remember.

322
00:21:47,307 --> 00:21:48,607
I've been in a daze.

323
00:21:48,607 --> 00:21:53,287
I've been living in a daze ever since that day.

324
00:21:53,287 --> 00:21:55,647
I couldn't find anything else to do.

325
00:21:57,847 --> 00:21:58,987
Nothing at all.

326
00:21:58,987 --> 00:22:09,687
When it was time to go, Akari gave me some leftover rice and chicken to take home with me.

327
00:22:10,387 --> 00:22:13,087
Be sure to put it in the fridge as soon as you get home.

328
00:22:13,447 --> 00:22:15,407
You can heat it up in the microwave later.

329
00:22:15,987 --> 00:22:17,727
Come back after your match on Monday.

330
00:22:18,007 --> 00:22:18,887
We'd love to see you.

331
00:22:18,887 --> 00:22:25,087
That'll be the last day of Obon, and we'll make more food.

332
00:22:26,047 --> 00:22:27,727
It's nice having company over.

333
00:22:27,727 --> 00:22:32,607
I thought I heard Akari say, it'll be a good distraction.

334
00:22:33,487 --> 00:22:36,367
But her voice was so soft, I can't be sure.

335
00:22:44,767 --> 00:22:48,827
On the way home as I crossed back over the bridge, the wind was strong.

336
00:22:48,827 --> 00:22:55,027
But the leftovers felt warm against my body, almost soothing, like a small animal.

337
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:37,071
Your old rival is in there waiting for you and he looks so intense!

338
00:24:37,611 --> 00:24:40,151
You're late, Kiriyama. I was getting tired of waiting.

339
00:24:40,351 --> 00:24:42,351
Excuse me, is the AC on?

340
00:24:42,871 --> 00:24:46,091
Compared to that department store roof, this place is a paradise.

341
00:24:46,831 --> 00:24:47,651
Shall we continue?

342
00:24:48,251 --> 00:24:50,391
Last piece of the fried chicken.

343
00:24:51,191 --> 00:24:52,791
One, two, three!

344
00:24:53,211 --> 00:24:56,551
Don't miss the next episode of March Comes In Like a Lion!

345
00:24:57,151 --> 00:24:58,171
We'll see you then!

346
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:30,991
We'll see you then!

